{
  "name": "m21mix_xl1",
  "description": "E41's stage on rows of 262,144 tokens (2026-11-27), read after the 64k stage. No model of ours was ever trained on a row longer than 65,536 tokens; the released 150M models find a planted number at 64k and never at 256k. One phase, `long`, at 262,144 tokens: single documents of at least that length (books, open-access academic books, US government publications: rule `doc`, 40 % of the tokens), planted-fact recall rows over several books in a row (recall_256k from scripts/build_reasoning_rows.py --only recall_256k: 25 %), and packed rows that keep the shorter skills alive (PDFs, code repositories, arXiv papers, and the 64k multi-hop and lookup rows, four to a row: rule `stream`, each document read within itself, 35 %). Every source except recall_256k is m21mix_v2's, shard for shard (the same specs, the same held-out documents), so a full build copies them and builds only the new set. SmolLM2 tokenizer.",
  "tokenizer": "HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M",
  "vocab_size": 49152,
  "eot": 0,
  "shard_tokens": 100000000,
  "defaults": {
    "val_fraction": 0.005,
    "val_tokens": 2000000,
    "val_min_docs": 40,
    "min_chars_per_token": 2.0
  },
  "sources": [
    {
